          "id": "occurrence-3044fc3912e5b79375dac5b2cc343e034c8c51db854d295b6a5d152918e806e4-a5acec3f06035bfb",
          "judge": "openai-codex/gpt-5.6-luna",
          "quote_span": "ED announced that while states may not deny free public K-12 education on the basis of immigration status under Plyler v. Doe , 457 U.S. 202 (1982), ED would apply the public benefits restrictions to adult education, career and technical education, and preschool programs administered by ED so long as such benefits are not protected under Plyler as part of a “basic” public education.",
